\section{\texttt{userland/sshcrypto.c}: the cryptography, with plain types}
\label{src:sshcrypto.c}

The functions below are all that the protocol needs. They are thin wrappers around BearSSL; a call each, no state of the library
leaks out. The random number generator is BearSSL's HMAC\_DRBG, seeded for every connection with 32 bytes from the hardware generator of
the kernel ([[getrandom]], the system call of the TLS chapter).

